  },
  "question": {
    "text": "A particle starts from rest and traverses a distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></math> with uniform acceleration, then moves uniformly over a further distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></math> and finally comes to rest after moving a further distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi></math> under uniform retardation. Assuming entire motion to be rectilinear motion, the ratio of average speed over the journey to the maximum speed on its way is"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>4</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>2</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></math>,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> be the time taken by the particles to cover the distance <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi></math> respectively. Let <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi></math> be the velocity of the particle at <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>&nbsp;i.e, maximum velocity. The particle moves with uniform acceleration from <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>.<br /><br />For motion from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></math> to <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></math>.<br /><br />Average velocity <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math><br /><br />Time taken,&nbsp;&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\"><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mfrac></math><br /><br />Particle moves with uniform retardation from&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> TO&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">D</mi></math>,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>V</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mi>v</mi><mi>g</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>v</mi></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math><br /><br />Time taken ,<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>(</mo><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac><mo>)</mo></mrow></mfrac></math><br /><br />Total time =&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math><br /><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mi>v</mi></mfrac><mo>+</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><mi>v</mi><mn>2</mn></mfrac></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>20</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mi>v</mi></mfrac></math><br /><br />Average Velocity over=&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mfrac bevelled=\"true\"><mrow><mn>20</mn><mi>x</mi></mrow><mi>v</mi></mfrac></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac><mi>v</mi></math><br />&nbsp;Required Ratio =&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>Average</mi><mo>Speed</mo></mrow><mi>v</mi></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>3</mn><mn>5</mn></mfrac></math>"
  }
}